IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tel-types`
IMPORT `tel-consumer`
IMPORT `tel-levy`

-- Telecommunications Act 2001 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Telecommunications position` HAS
    `Chorus may stop the copper service`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party may appeal the determination`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `interest on late levy`                             IS A NUMBER

@ref ss 14, 69AC-69AD, 242-244; Schedule 2A
@export default The consumer-facing position under the Telecommunications Act 2001 (NZ): whether Chorus may stop supplying an end-user's copper service (ss 69AC-69AD, Schedule 2A); whether a party may appeal a dispute determination (ss 242-244); and the interest on a levy paid late (s 14). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Copper service`  @desc The copper service facts
      p IS A `Dispute party`  @desc The dispute party facts
      l IS A `Levy payment`  @desc The levy payment facts
      days IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days
GIVETH A `Telecommunications position`
`the telecommunications position for` c `, dispute party` p `, levy` l `, non-working days` days MEANS
    `Telecommunications position` WITH
        `Chorus may stop the copper service`        IS `Chorus may stop supplying the copper service` c
        `the party may appeal the determination`    IS `the party may appeal the determination` p days
        `interest on late levy`                     IS `the interest on late levy` l
